 succeeded in 0ms:
   160	**Format.**
   161	
   162	> **Workflow Status** — Mode: `chat` — Active: Step 2 of 6
   163	
   164	| # | Step | State | Iter | Verdict |
   165	|---|---|---|---|---|
   166	| 1 | Configuration | `✓ Done` | — | — |
   167	| 2 | Ideation Loop | `▸ DISCUSSION` | `1 / 3` | — |
   168	| 3 | Preparation Loop | `… Pending` | — | — |
   169	| 4 | Planning Loop | `… Pending` | — | — |
   170	| 5 | Execution Loop | `… Pending` | — | — |
   171	| 6 | Wrap-up Loop | `… Pending` | — | — |
   172	
   173	> Active: Constructing the leader delegation prompt — scope, inputs, constraints, success criteria, references.
   174	
   175	**State values.**
   176	
   177	| State | Meaning |
   178	|---|---|
   179	| `… Pending` | Step not yet started |
   180	| `▸ DISCUSSION` / `▸ WORK` / `▸ EVALUATION` / `▸ MEMORIZATION` / `▸ ITER/EXIT` | Step active; current phase named (`WORK` is replaced by the loop's verb — `IDEATION`, `PLAN_DRAFT`, `EXECUTION`, `WRAPUP`) |
   181	| `↪ Revising` | `EVALUATION` returned `REVISE` and the loop is re-entering `DISCUSSION` (`iter` increments) |
   182	| `✓ Done` | Step completed via the `PASS` verdict path |
   183	| `⊘ Skipped` | Step bypassed without running `EVALUATION`. Triggered at loop entry by `skip: true` OR `maxIterations: 0` (two independent signals — see [§ Workflow State Machine](#workflow-state-machine) loop-entry resolution), OR mid-loop when `evaluate.mode == 'skip'` (loop ran `WORK` → `MEMORIZATION`, no verdict). The `Verdict` column stays `—`. |
   184	| `✗ Aborted` | `maxIterations` exhausted without `PASS` |
   185	
   186	**Field rules.**
   187	
   188	- **`#` and `Step`** — fixed (1–6; Configuration / Ideation Loop / Preparation Loop / Planning Loop / Execution Loop / Wrap-up Loop).
   189	- **`Iter`** — `{current} / {max}` while inside a loop; `—` for Configuration and pending steps.
   190	- **`Verdict`** — `—` until `EVALUATION` completes for the current iteration; then `PASS` / `REVISE` / `FAIL`. Cleared back to `—` on re-entry.
   191	- **`Active` line** — one sentence describing what the manager is doing right now: what is being constructed, which subagent is about to be spawned, what was just received. Omit between loops.
   192	- **Header line** — `Mode: chat | auto`; `Active: Step N of 6` (or `Active: — (between loops)` at boundaries).
   193	
   194	**Render points.**
   195	
   196	| Mode | Render before |
   197	|---|---|
   198	| Chat | Every AskUserQuestion (after `DISCUSSION`, after `EVALUATION`, at `ITER / EXIT`, at session end) |
   199	| Auto | Every loop exit (transition out of `ITER / EXIT`); every user-authority interrupt; whenever the user asks for status |
   200	
   201	The display is for the user — it is not state storage. The state machine itself is governed by the [Workflow State Machine](#workflow-state-machine) section; the display is a read-only projection.
   202	
   203	**Chat-mode rendering.** In Chat Mode the display uses a two-tier structure (session-level + per-task tier) backed by `state.json.workflow.chat.tasks[currentIndex]` (R3 lock, §6.7). The full Chat rendering spec — header form, body form, and a worked example showing a completed prior task plus the active task — lives in [`chat-mode.md § Status Display`](chat-mode.md). Auto-mode rendering is the existing 6-row table above; it is unchanged.
   204	
   205	---
   206	
   207	## Canonical session tree
   208	
   209	The on-disk layout every session materializes under `.gobbi/projects/{project-name}/sessions/{date}-{session-id}/`. The manager bootstraps each loop's `{rawdata, staging, evaluation, artifacts}` subdirs at loop entry; the assistant and evaluator write into them per their skills. This is the canonical shape; deviations are normalized going-forward by Wrap-up (see [`wrap-up/SKILL.md` § Non-standard session-subdir cleanup](../wrap-up/SKILL.md)).
   210	
   211	```
   212	sessions/{date}-{session-id}/
   213	├── session.json              ← per-session telemetry (manager init row 6 + assistant UPSERT)
   214	├── settings.json             ← resolved session config (cascade)
   215	├── state.json                ← per-session workflow state-machine file (manager init row 5.5; see § State persistence)
   216	├── session.json.lock         ← advisory write-lock guarding concurrent session.json writes (manager; safe to ignore on read)
   217	└── {loop}/                   ← loop ∈ ideation | preparation | planning | execution | wrap-up
   218	    ├── rawdata/              ← draft-iter{n}.md, transcript-iter{n}.jsonl, discussion-log.md, research/{slug}.md
   219	    │                            (the ONLY scratch surface — no separate tmp/ tier; resume/restore scratch lives here, not in restore/)
   220	    ├── staging/{...}/        ← typed-finding stagings (Wrap-up promotion source)
   221	    ├── evaluation/iter{n}/{claude,codex}/{perspective}.md + overall.md
   222	    └── artifacts/{free-filename}.md   ← PASS-only
   223	```
   224	
   225	**Session-root files.** `session.json` (telemetry), `settings.json` (resolved config), `state.json` (the workflow state-machine file — see [§ State persistence](#state-persistence)), and `session.json.lock` (advisory write-lock the manager creates / releases around each `session.json` write; not memory content — safe to ignore on read).
   226	
   227	**No `tmp/` scratch tier.** `{loop}/rawdata/` is the only scratch surface in the canonical tree. A `tmp/` dir or a `rawdata/restore/` sub-tier is non-canonical — resume / restore scratch lives directly in `rawdata/`. Wrap-up removes `tmp/` going-forward (see [`wrap-up/SKILL.md`](../wrap-up/SKILL.md)).
   228	
   229	### Per-task Execution layout (the quartet)
   230	
   231	The Execution loop is per-task. Each task lives under `execution/task-{NN}/` and carries the **full quartet** — `{rawdata, staging, evaluation, artifacts}`:
   232	
   233	```
   234	execution/
   235	├── staging/{...}/            ← loop-level (cross-task) staging
   236	└── task-{NN}/
   237	    ├── rawdata/draft-iter{n}.md, transcript-iter{n}.jsonl
   238	    ├── staging/{...}/
   239	    ├── evaluation/iter{n}/{claude,codex}/{perspective}.md + overall.md
   240	    └── artifacts/{free-filename}.md
   241	```
   242	
   243	Every `task-{NN}/` gets the full quartet. A task with only `evaluation/` (missing rawdata / staging / artifacts) is an incomplete task layout — the quartet is required unless a task is documented eval-only.
   244	
   245	### Per-perspective evaluation file naming
   246	
   247	Evaluation outputs are named `evaluation/iter{n}/{system}/{perspective}.md` where `{system} ∈ {claude, codex}` and `{perspective}` is the **bare** perspective name from the fixed 7-vocabulary — `project`, `structure`, `performance`, `aesthetics`, `usage`, `consistency`, `risk` — plus `overall.md`. **Bare names only**: no `pN-` positional prefix, and the **same 7-perspective vocabulary on both systems** so cross-system reconciliation pairs files 1:1. The 7-perspective vocabulary is owned by [`evaluation/SKILL.md`](../evaluation/SKILL.md); the manager's spawn / reconciliation orchestration is in [`workflow/evaluation.md`](workflow/evaluation.md).
   248	
   249	---
   250	
   251	## Workflow State Machine
   252	
   253	In Auto Mode the state machine runs linearly across the six steps. In Chat Mode it dispatches a per-task slice meta-loop between Configuration and Wrap-up; see [`chat-mode.md §3 — Workflow`](chat-mode.md) for the Chat-specific per-slice procedure and [`chat-mode.md §8.2 — Per-task state-transition table`](chat-mode.md) for the state-transition table. The rest of this section describes the loop-internal phase mechanics (DISCUSSION → WORK → EVALUATION → MEMORIZATION → ITER/EXIT) shared by both modes.
   254	
   255	> **Loop-entry Skipped resolution (two independent signals).** A workflow step resolves to
   256	> `state: Skipped` at loop entry when **either** `skip: true` **OR** `maxIterations: 0` is set
   257	> for that step — the two are independent signals, and either one alone is sufficient. A Skipped
   258	> step runs no DISCUSSION / WORK / EVALUATION / MEMORIZATION rows, emits no `FAIL` or `Aborted`
   259	> verdict, and stamps `{state: "Skipped", iterations: []}`. The `maxIterations: 0` path (the
   260	> original "R1 lock") is retained and coexists with the explicit `skip` boolean; `skip: true` is
   261	> the preferred explicit signal, `maxIterations: 0` remains valid for back-compatibility. This
   262	> is distinct from `evaluate.mode: "skip"`, which skips only the EVALUATION phase (the loop still
   263	> runs WORK → MEMORIZATION), not the whole step.
   264	
   265	This section specifies the phase mechanics shared by steps 2-6. The manager moves between states only when each state's postcondition is met.
   266	
   267	### State persistence
   268	
   269	The manager maintains state in a per-session `state.json` file.
   270	
   271	| Field | Value |
   272	|---|---|
   273	| Location | `.gobbi/projects/{project-name}/sessions/{date}-{session-id}/state.json` |
   274	| Initial template | [`templates/state.template.json`](templates/state.template.json) |
   275	| Writer | manager (the manager agent) |
   276	| Update points | every state transition (`DISCUSSION` → `WORK`, `WORK` → `EVALUATION`, `EVALUATION` → `MEMORIZATION`, `MEMORIZATION` → `ITER / EXIT`, and the inter-step transitions at loop exits) |
   277	| Reader | manager — used to recover position after `/clear`, `/compact`, or session resume; also projected into the [Workflow Status Display](#workflow-status-display) |
   278	| Status semantics | `state` is one of `Pending` / `Active` / `Revising` / `Done` / `Skipped` / `Aborted`; when `Active`, the `phase` field names the current state (`DISCUSSION`, `WORK`'s loop verb, `EVALUATION`, `MEMORIZATION`, `ITER/EXIT`) |
   279	| Schema shape | `workflow` is keyed by step name — `configuration`, `ideation`, `preparation`, `planning`, `execution`, `wrap-up` — matching the `workflow.{step}` keys in `settings.json`. Each `state.json` entry carries `state`, `verdict`, `iter`, `maxIterations`, `phase`. (The `settings.json` per-step object additionally carries a `skip` boolean alongside `discuss` / `evaluate` / `maxIterations`; the state-machine entry derives `Skipped` from it at loop entry per the loop-entry resolution above. The `state.json` schema itself does NOT gain a `skip` key — only settings does.) The current active step is derived (the entry whose `state` is `Active` or `Revising`); there is no separate `active` key. The display order (Configuration → Ideation → Preparation → Planning → Execution → Wrap-up) is fixed by convention; the manager renders the [Workflow Status Display](#workflow-status-display) in that order regardless of object iteration. **Chat sessions additionally carry `workflow.chat.tasks[]`** — see the schema below. |
   280	| `workflow.chat.tasks[]` schema (additive — Chat sessions only) | Present in both `state.json` and `session.json` when `settings.mode == "chat"`. Auto sessions leave this array empty. Each entry: `taskNo` (zero-padded ordinal), `slug` (subject-descriptive kebab-case), `startedAt`, `finishedAt`, and per-loop sub-records `ideation` / `preparation` / `planning` / `execution` (same `{state, verdict, iter, maxIterations, phase, iterations[]}` shape as the top-level `workflow.{loop}` entries — same parser, different path), plus `taskRecord: { path, writtenAt }`. The `preparation` sub-record carries `state: "Skipped"` by default (R1). **Templates**: `templates/state.template.json` and `templates/session.template.json` both gain `workflow.chat: { tasks: [] }` — auto sessions ship the same templates and leave the array empty. The `state.json` variant is the live state-machine projection (R3); the `session.json` variant archives final iter + verdict per slice (R2). |
   281	
   282	### Loop states
   283	
   284	| State | Precondition | Owner | Action | Postcondition (artifact) |
   285	|---|---|---|---|---|
   286	| `DISCUSSION` | Loop entered with input from the prior step, OR re-entered from `ITER / EXIT` after `REVISE` / `FAIL` | manager | Construct the delegation prompt for the owning specialist; in Chat Mode, confirm with the user; spawn the specialist via the Agent tool (the full delegation prompt is captured in the parent transcript's tool_use entry — no separate file is written) | Specialist agent spawned; delegation prompt persisted in the parent's transcript |
   287	| `WORK` | Specialist spawned in `DISCUSSION` | owning specialist (`leader` / `executor` / `assistant`) | Execute the loop's work per the delegation prompt received via the Agent tool | Loop's work artifact |
   288	| `EVALUATION` | Work artifact exists; `workflow.{step}.evaluate.mode != 'skip'` | evaluator subagents (independent of the work owner) | Multi-perspective review per the evaluation policy | Aggregated verdict: `PASS` / `REVISE` / `FAIL` |
   289	| `MEMORIZATION` | `EVALUATION` complete OR `EVALUATION` skipped per policy | `assistant` subagent | Write session staging for this iteration; project-memory promotion only in Wrap-up | Memory writes complete |
   290	| `ITER / EXIT` | `MEMORIZATION` complete | manager | Decide based on verdict and budget — continue (transition to `DISCUSSION` with `iter += 1`) or exit (loop closed; surface output to next step) | Loop continues OR loop closed |
   291	
   292	`iter` starts at `0` on loop entry. `maxIterations` is read from `workflow.{step}.maxIterations` (default `3`).
   293	
   294	If `evaluate.mode == 'skip'`, the loop bypasses `EVALUATION` and proceeds `WORK` → `MEMORIZATION` → `ITER / EXIT` on the first pass; the absent verdict is treated as `Skipped` at `ITER / EXIT`.
   295	
   296	### Verdict aggregation
   297	
   298	| Evaluator verdicts | Aggregated verdict |
   299	|---|---|
   300	| All `PASS` | `PASS` |
   301	| Any `REVISE`, no `FAIL` | `REVISE` |
   302	| Any `FAIL` | `FAIL` |
   303	
